# Change discipline

- Reproduce a bug and state its root cause before changing code. If you can't reproduce it, say so.
- Make the smallest diff that solves the task. Don't rewrite, rename, reformat, restructure or "clean up" working code outside the task. Don't swap libraries or upgrade dependencies unless asked.
- Read the callers of anything you change; keep props, function signatures, API shapes and column names stable, or update every caller.
- Don't delete code you don't understand; ask.
- Destructive database or git operations need explicit user permission.
- Verify before claiming done: run build, type check, lint and tests where they exist, and report the actual results. If you can't verify something, give the user exact manual steps.
- End with: files changed, what each change does, how to test, and any actions the user must take (migrations, env vars, dashboard settings, redeploy). List other problems you noticed without fixing them.
- Suggest a git commit after each working step.
